B", "keywords": ["GLB", "glTF", "Viewer", "Portfolio"], "long_description": "Bring Your 3D Models to Life in VR\n\nDo you want to view your 3D creations on your Meta Quest headset without the headache? Seek no further\u2014Glimpse glTF is here to help.\n\nBefore this app, getting a 3D model onto the Quest to simply \"look at it\" was surprisingly difficult. Typing long URLs into a VR browser with controllers is frustrating, and copy-pasting isn't always an option. Glimpse glTF solves this by focusing on a streamlined, local-first workflow.\n\nWhy Glimpse glTF? We exclusively support .GLB (glTF) files. Unlike FBX or OBJ, GLB is a modern, single-file format that embeds all your textures and materials. This means no missing textures and no messy folder structures\u2014just one file that works.\n\nKey Features:\n\nFull PBR Support: View your models as intended with Albedo, Metalness, Gloss/Roughness, and Lightmaps.\n\nAnimation Ready: Play back embedded animations instantly.\n\nLocal Loading: No internet streaming required during viewing. Load high-fidelity models instantly from your device storage.\n\nHow to use Glimpse glTF: This app reads directly from your headset's Downloads folder. You can get your files there easily using methods you already know:\n\nGoogle Drive/Cloud: Open the Quest Browser, log into your Drive, and download your .glb file.\n\nSketchfab: Browse Sketchfab in the Quest Browser and download models directly.\n\nUSB Transfer: Connect your headset to your PC/Mac via cable and drop your files into the specific Downloads folder.\n\nOnce the file is on your headset, just op", "short_description": "The easiest way to preview GLB models in VR. View local files with full support for textures, PBR materials, and animations directly from your Downloads folder."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://patrickgoud.com/pages/glimpse-glb-privacy-support", "developer_terms_of_service_url": null, "publisher_name": "Patrick Goud", "supp